# Deploy desktop, macOS and sandbox files only to the machines that use them: no
# `.chezmoiremove` entries here. Verified against a scratch --destination that a target BOTH
# ignored (home/.chezmoiignore) and listed here is a silent no-op — chezmoi drops an ignored
# path from the removal set as well as from the deploy set, so an entry here would read as if
# it worked and would not. The cleanup instead runs live, in
# .chezmoiscripts/{os-linux,os-windows,os-darwin}/run_onchange_after_cleanup-host-gated-files.*,
# the same way a systemd unit's dangling-unit cleanup does (#688) — this is that mechanism
# applied to plain files and directories instead of units.

